BT /F1 10 Tf 60 770 Td (- all dollar amounts, copied exactly as written in the text) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 60 751 Td (- the storage variant each amount belongs to, if the offer has a variant table) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 60 732 Td (- whether an amount is monthly) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 60 713 Td (- a short one-line description) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48 688 Td (The prompt is strict on one point: use only facts from the text, never calculate or round) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48 675 Td (anything, and return null when something is not stated. I also put one example from the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48 662 Td (assignment brief in the prompt, as a few-shot example.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48 637 Td (I saved the results in llm_cache.json. Run the notebook again and it does not call the API for) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48 624 Td (offers it has already done.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 48 598 Td (Checking the LLM output for made-up numbers) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48 576 Td (This was the part I did not want to skip. Every amount the LLM returned gets checked against) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48 563 Td (the original text. If an amount does not appear in the text, it gets dropped. Unknown) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48 550 Td (categories get dropped too. In the final run, all the extracted amounts passed this check,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48 537 Td (which was reassuring, but the check stays in place either way.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 48 511 Td (Applying the Python rules) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48 489 Td (For each product and each line type, the rules are:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48 464 Td (Line type check. An offer is used only if the current line type is in its eligible list. The) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48 451 Td ($800 switcher offer, for example, shows up only in New Line rows.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48 426 Td (Variant check. Device discounts are taken only for the matching storage variant. The 1 TB model) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48 413 Td (gets $628.36, not the 256 GB amount of $660.36. Before comparing, I normalise "256 GB" and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48 400 Td ("256GB" so a spacing difference does not break the match.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48 375 Td (No double counting. Each amount goes into only one column. A monthly amount, for example) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48 362 Td ($5.56/mo., is not used when the total of $200 is available.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48 337 Td (Finance offer. For a New Line it is the welcome bonus plus the yearly statement credit plus the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48 324 Td (bill discount: $200 + $240 + $10 = $450. For an Upgrade it is only the recurring parts: $240 +) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48 311 Td ($10 = $250. I did not add the $20 per billing cycle credit again, because it is already part of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48 298 Td (the $240 per year.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48 273 Td (Money is handled with Python Decimal, not float, so the decimals do not get rounded away by) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48 260 Td (binary floating point.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 48 234 Td (Writing the output) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48 212 Td (Before saving, the CSV gets checked: it must have exactly 2 rows per product, and exactly the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48 199 Td (29 required columns. Missing values are left blank.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 48 171 Td (4. When the API pushed back) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48 148 Td (A few things went wrong while I was building this, and the pipeline had to cope with them:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 60 123 Td (- Server busy \(503\), timeouts and malformed JSON: retried up to 3 times, with longer waits) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 60 110 Td (each time, 2s, then 4s, then 8s.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 60 91 Td (- Rate limit per minute \(429\): wait 60 seconds and retry.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 60 72 Td (- Daily quota finished \(429, per day\): retrying will not help there, so the pipeline switches) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 60 59 Td (to the next Gemini model in a candidate list.) Tj ET
